OL,1,V7w3s7s35E                         G7/13
OL,2,V55555555C#415,000 DAMAGES
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5COVER HOSPITAL BLUNDER
OL,5, The mother of a baby who suffered brain
OL,6, damage because of a hospital blunder
OL,7, was awarded #415,000 in the High Court.
OL,9, Ruth Husbands's baby Emma was delivered
OL,10, stillborn after midwives at King's
OL,11, College Hospital, London, failed to
OL,12, spot her weak heartbeat in time.
OL,14, A junior paediatrician saved Emma's
OL,15, life after her heart stopped. She is
OL,16, now five but will never progress
OL,17, beyond the mental age of seven.
OL,19, Ms Husbands, 30, of Stockwell, London,
OL,20, said:"No amount of money can compensate
OL,21, for what Emma could have been."
OL,22,G]D This ORACLE page is from 29-01-90
OL,23,G] AMuch more at: teletextarchive.com
