OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G8/13
OL,2,V55555555CHILLSBOROUGH: IT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CCOULD HAPPEN AGAIN
OL,5, A disaster like Hillsborough could
OL,6, happen again, says Lord Justice Taylor
OL,7, in his report into last year's tragedy
OL,8, in which 95 people died.
OL,10, There is a blight over the game because
OL,11, of old grounds, poor facilities,
OL,12, hooliganism, excessive drinking and
OL,13, poor leadership, he says.CAlso p112/113
OL,15, Football authorities, club directors
OL,16, and players are all criticised by the
OL,17, judge, who says years of "muddling
OL,18, through on a wing and prayer" must end.
OL,20, It was chilling to hear several clubs
OL,21, say "it couldn't have happened here"
OL,22, even after Hillsborough.         C>>>>>
OL,23,F]DFrom 29-01-90 / teletextarchive.com
