OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769717123
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G9/13
OL,2,V55555555CTAYLOR SEEKS NEW OFFENCES,
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSUGGESTS 'TAGGING'
OL,4,         C
OL,5, The main findings of the Taylor report
OL,6, into the Hillsborough disaster are:
OL,8,S$GGrave doubts about ID card system
OL,10,S$GAll-seater stadiums in English First
OL,11,   and Second Divisions and Scottish
OL,12,   Premier by August 1994.
OL,14, New offences of:
OL,15,S$GThrowing a missile
OL,16,S$GChanting obscene or racist abuse
OL,17,S$GInvading the pitch without reason
OL,19, The report suggests:
OL,20,S$GElectronic "tagging" of hooligans
OL,21,S$GA review of police tactics
OL,22,S$GPerimeter fences limited to 2.2metres
OL,23,F]DFrom 29-01-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
