PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769717123
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                         G10/13
OL,2,V55555555CTAYLOR'S GRAVE DOUBTS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CON SOCCER ID CARDS
OL,4,         C
OL,5, Lord Justice Taylor expresses grave
OL,6, doubts about the feasibility of the
OL,7, Government's proposed soccer ID card
OL,8, scheme and serious misgivings on safety
OL,10, It would only increase the danger of
OL,11, crushing at turnstiles because of time
OL,12, taken checking cards with crowd noise
OL,13, from inside making fans more anxious.
OL,15, It was "merely wishful thinking" that
OL,16, hooligans turned away with no ID cards
OL,17, would not cause trouble elsewhere.
OL,19, Preoccupation with hooligan control had
OL,20, meant lack of concern for the safety of
OL,21, spectators and segregation only bred an
OL,22, "us and them" attitude, he says. C>>>>>
OL,23,F]DFrom 29-01-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769717123
OL,1,V7w3s7s35                         G11/13
OL,2,V55555555CTAYLOR ROUNDS ON
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CFA AND LEAGUE
OL,4,         C
OL,5, The Taylor report attacks "poor leader-
OL,6, ship" and says the Football Association
OL,7, and Football League have not seen it as
OL,8, their duty to offer clubs safety advice
OL,10, They were as much concerned to avoid
OL,11, pitch invasions because they interfered
OL,12, with the smooth progress of the fixture
OL,13, list and led to criticism and penalty
OL,14, from the European football authorities.
OL,16, It could not help promote good
OL,17, behaviour if a club chairman was shown
OL,18, presenting a cheque to a player fined
OL,19, the same sum for pitch misbehaviour.
OL,21, And on the pitch itself, Corinthian
OL,22, Casual standards of cool self-control
OL,23, had long since departed, he said.C>>>>>
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769717123
OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                        G12/13
OL,2,V55555555CGOVT CONFIRMS IT
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CWILL DROP ID CARDS
OL,5, The Government will not go ahead with
OL,6, plans for a soccer ID card scheme, Home
OL,7, Secretary David Waddington confirmed.
OL,9, But he told MPs that legislation paving
OL,10, the way for it would stay on the
OL,11, statute book.
OL,13, He pledged to act quickly to set up a
OL,14, football licensing authoritiy which
OL,15, would require all-seater stadiums.
OL,17, "Squalid conditions" at football
OL,18, grounds encouraged squalid behaviour.
OL,20, Labour's Roy Hattersley said if the
OL,21, Taylor report was sensibly applied it
OL,22, would be a basis for improvement.
OL,23,F]DFrom 29-01-90 / teletextarchive.com
