OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769717123
OL,1,V7w3s7s35E                        G13/13
OL,2,V55555555CGALES AND FLOODS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CHIT WESTERN ENGLAND
OL,5, The west of England has taken a second
OL,6, battering from gales in five days, with
OL,7, winds near 100mph and the River Severn
OL,8, at its highest level for 20 years.
OL,10, Falmouth coastguards reported one gust
OL,11, of 95mph while ships were sheltering in
OL,12, both Falmouth Bay and St Ives Bay.
OL,14, Power officials said 36,000 homes in
OL,15, Devon, Cornwall, Avon and Somerset were
OL,16, without electricity for a fourth
OL,17, successive day.
OL,19, Homes in Worcester were flooded, with
OL,20, the race course, cricket ground, roads
OL,21, and fields under several feet of water
OL,22, because of melting snow and heavy rain.
OL,23,F]DFrom 29-01-90 / teletextarchive.com
